If you stop, look, and listen, you can almost hear things grow;
You can find music wherever you go.
I hear a symphony of city traffic;
There are horns blowing; there are heels clicking.
Hear those trash cans rattling as the sun begins to rise;
All you have to do is listen to ...

Hear the world's music turning.
Can't you hear the sweet sound of the world turning?
If you stop, look, and listen, you can almost hear things grow;
You can find music wherever you go.
The wind has a special song for each and every day;
It makes the waves dance and the thunder clap.
Now, don't just ignore it—there's a concert all around you;
All you have to do is listen to ...

Hear the world's music turning.
Can't you hear the sweet sound of the world turning?
If you stop, look, and listen, you can almost hear things grow;
